---
source: crates/ostro/tests/cli_p11.rs
expression: "help(&[\"rerun\"])"
---
Rerun a terminal run from a cut (a new run; effects after the cut re-execute)

Usage: ostro rerun [OPTIONS] <--from-step <NAME[#N]>|--from-seq <N>> <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>  Source run id (terminal)

Options:
      --from-step <NAME[#N]>
          Cut before the N-th (1-based, default 1) execution of step NAME: `NAME` or `NAME#N`
      --from-seq <N>
          Cut at journal sequence number N (events before N are copied)
      --version <active|source|N>
          Version to execute: `active` (server default), `source` or a number
      --idempotency-key <IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>
          Dedupe key: the same key returns the same rerun
      --dry-run
          Validate only: the server runs the cut analysis and replay check, starts nothing
      --server <SERVER>
          Server URL [env: OSTRO_SERVER=] [default: http://127.0.0.1:7700]
      --json
          Print the REST response body as JSON
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Per-request timeout (friendly duration; a long-poll adds its wait) [default: 30s]
      --ca-file <PEM>
          PEM CA certificate to trust for an https:// server instead of the platform roots (e.g. the cluster CA `<data_dir>/tls/ca.crt` behind a self-signed listener) [env: OSTRO_CA_FILE=]
  -h, --help
          Print help
